# Docker volumes (local bind mounts, if any)
.data/

# Database dumps from scripts/backup-restore-drill.sh.
#
# These are full copies of every logical database, so they contain real member
# data - names, contact details, children's records, consent history. Committing
# one would put personal data in git history, which is close to the hardest
# place on this platform to remove it from, and would defeat the erasure the
# platform goes to some trouble to honour.
.backup-drill/

# Smoke-suite output. Written by scripts/smoke-through-gateway.sh when its output
# is redirected; it names real members and tokens from the run.
.smoke.log

# The tenant-isolation probe writes here. Same reason as .smoke.log: it is a
# run of a check against a local stack, not a fact about the repository.
.probe.log

# Backend test-suite output from a full run across every solution.
.backend-tests.log
